From 49fadd9db8239c351e552b70d8f49e2b62ea9b68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vova Zakharov <vzakharov@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 02:18:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: let a repository add its own estimate roles, graded or
 not

An adopting repository could only estimate in the roles rates.json ships,
and editing that file collides with every sync of it. A repository now keeps
its own roles in .claude/costs/rates.repo.json, beside the table and in its
shape. The overlay may only add: an entry the table already rates at another
multiplier raises, so no row is re-rated without the table saying so.

Either file may also carry an `ungraded` table: roles that take no grade,
worth hours times the role's own multiplier. Such a part is written as
`--part <hours> <role> <why>` and stored with a null grade; checked() refuses
a grade on an ungraded role and a missing one on a graded role. The hours
table files ungraded hours in an `ungraded` column after the grades.

estimate.py, report.py and check_estimates.py load the table through
load_rates(); the estimate notice and check_estimates list ungraded roles
only when there are some, so the shipped text is unchanged. report.py
--all-my-repos reads each ledger's overlay off GitHub as well, since a row
there may name a role only its own repository rates.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PUYJksvzRTYbgjWSg2ypty
